  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "Maister Skills are the most powerful abilities in the game and require completing specific NPC questlines, not levelling—find each Maister NPC in their starting location within the first 15 in-game days before they migrate.",
      "Pawn inclinations determine combat AI behaviour more than equipment or skills—a Pawn with Straightforward and Acquisitor inclinations seeks items during combat; Challenger and Nexus inclinations provide the most consistent combat support.",
      "Carry weight is the single most impactful stat for exploration efficiency—the Logistician Augment (Fighter Vocation rank 9) grants +3 kg carrying capacity, and the Robustness augment (+4 kg) stacks with it. Distribute heavy items across all four party members to maximise total carry.",
      "Wakestones revive the Arisen at full HP at any death location and can be used unlimited times. Wakestone farming route: Bakbattahl market (2 per shop refresh cycle) + Gran Soren Riftstones (5 per rest cycle). Never progress far into the endgame without 5+ Wakestones banked.",
      "Time-based events and shopkeeper inventories reset on a 7-day in-game cycle—long rests (inn stays or camping) advance time; micromanage rest frequency to align with shop restocks for rare material farming."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "マイスタースキルはゲーム最強の技で、レベルではなくNPCクエストライン完了で習得する。各マイスターNPCは最初の15ゲーム内日数以内に初期位置で見つけないと移動してしまう。",
      "ポーンの傾向はスキルや装備より戦闘AIに影響する。「直攻め」と「収集」傾向は戦闘中に素材を拾いに行く。「挑戦者」と「結び目」傾向が最も安定した戦闘補助を提供する。",
      "携行重量は探索効率に最も影響するステータス。「物流家」強化（ファイター職ランク9）で+3kg、「強靭」強化で+4kgが積み重なる。重いアイテムは全4人に分散して最大携行量を確保する。",
      "覚者の石は任意の死亡地点でHP全回復で復活し、無制限に使える。ファーミングルート：バクバタール市場（ショップ更新サイクルごとに2個）＋グランソーレン霊器石（休息サイクルごとに5個）。終盤に進む前に必ず5個以上ストックする。",
      "時間依存イベントとショップ在庫は7日間のゲーム内サイクルでリセットされる。宿屋または野営での長期休憩が時間を進める。ショップの再入荷タイミングに合わせて休息頻度を調整する。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Vocation Selection and Early Augments",
        "body": "Start as Fighter for the first 5 hours to unlock Shield Drum (Rank 4, stuns nearby enemies—useful for every subsequent vocation) and the Robustness augment (+4 kg). Then transition to Thief or Archer depending on playstyle. Avoid Mage as a starting vocation: healing spell unlocks require Rank 6 and the Mage kit underperforms until then. Warrior is the strongest late-game vocation but has the steepest learning curve in the first dungeon."
      },
      {
        "title": "Main Pawn Specialisation",
        "body": "Your Main Pawn's Vocation determines party role: Mage Pawns handle healing (mandatory—always have one Mage Pawn in party), Sorcerer Pawns for AoE, Warrior Pawns for stagger. Equip the Main Pawn with the Item Deployment augment (Merchant vocation) regardless of their combat vocation—this enables auto-use of healing items during combat without player input, functioning as a passive healing system."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Combat Against Large Monsters",
        "body": "Dragon's Dogma 2's signature mechanic is climbing large enemies to attack weak points. Stamina management while climbing is critical: heavy equipment reduces climbing stamina to near zero. Maintain light-medium load (under 60% carry weight) to sustain 8–10 seconds of climbing. Weak points on Griffins are the wings' shoulder joints; on Cyclops, the eye; on Drakes, the chest and hind leg junction. Targeting these reduces HP faster than body attacks by 1.8–2.4× depending on the enemy."
      },
      {
        "title": "Battahl Region Navigation",
        "body": "Battahl requires a Travel Pass obtained from the Checkpoint Rest Town questline—attempting to sneak through the border triggers high-level guard encounters. Once inside, the Battahl Cavern system provides direct shortcuts to major areas that are 3–5 minutes faster than surface routes. The Battahl Sphinx encounter has time-sensitive riddles—they expire if you rest at an inn before answering, so complete the Sphinx riddle sequence in a single continuous session."
      },
      {
        "title": "Maister Quest Priority",
        "body": "Priority Maister locations for early unlocks: Warrior Maister (Brokkr) at Volcanic Island Camp—available from day 3 but requires 4,000 gold donation to unlock conversation. Mystic Spearhand Maister (Sigurd) at Melve—triggered by speaking to him before the Dragon attack on the village. Trickster Maister (Luz) at Checkpoint Rest Town—expires after completing the main story arc. All three have window-based availability; check all three within the first in-game week."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Dragon Confrontation",
        "body": "The Dragon fight proceeds in two phases. Phase 1: target the heart (visible chest glow) with heavy attacks from the Warrior or concentrated arrow volleys from Archer. Phase 2 triggers at 50% HP when the Dragon becomes airborne. Use the Mystic Spearhand Maister skill (Vortex Spear) to pull the Dragon back to ground level. Keeping the Dragon grounded throughout phase 2 cuts the fight duration in half versus an aerial-only encounter."
      },
      {
        "title": "True Ending: The Unmoored World",
        "body": "The Unmoored World (NG+ equivalent) activates after defeating the Dragon and refusing the sacrifice option. In this phase, a Rift Condensation timer counts down—complete all marked red beacons before the timer depletes or NPCs begin permanently dying. Priority order: Vernworth beacon first (5 unique questlines attached), Bakbattahl beacon second, then Harve Village. Save Wakestones for the final confrontation with the True Dragon, which deals physical damage only and requires a minimum of 3 Wakestones for most builds."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Dismissing Hired Pawns from the Rift without reviewing their inclinations and bestiary knowledge—a Pawn with Dragon/Sphinx knowledge in its bestiary provides combat hints that save significant trial-and-error time.",
      "Carrying all items personally instead of distributing across Pawns—exceeding 60% carry weight reduces stamina regeneration rate by 35%, directly impacting climbing and sprint performance.",
      "Missing Maister NPC windows—three of the nine Maister NPCs have story-locked availability windows that permanently close after specific main story quests. Check Maister locations every 3–4 main quests.",
      "Resting at inns without completing time-sensitive riddles or events—each 7-day rest cycle advances quests that have in-progress timers, potentially skipping reward stages.",
      "Entering the Unmoored World without banking rare crafting materials—inventory transfer to the Unmoored World is limited; priority items to bank first: Dragonforged upgrade stones, Wakestones (10+), and Maister skill items."
    ],
